From 4b26e6130f722ae82e108a8df25cc86e48e2a0e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:18:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Fix documentation of `SCOTCH_graphPartOvlView()`

The reference to the section of `SCOTCH_graphPartOvl()` was written
as a `\label`, which defined the label a second time, so that the
references to that section elsewhere in the manual pointed to the
new section, and printed nothing in place. The `partnbr` and
`parttab` parameters are `const`, as in `library.h`.
---
 doc/src/scotch/s_l.tex | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/src/scotch/s_l.tex b/doc/src/scotch/s_l.tex
index 04d24511..33077ff8 100644
--- a/doc/src/scotch/s_l.tex
+++ b/doc/src/scotch/s_l.tex
@@ -4079,8 +4079,8 @@ filled, but its contents are not significant.
 
 {\tt\begin{tabular}{l@{}ll}
 int SCOTCH\_graphPartOvlView ( & const SCOTCH\_Graph * & grafptr, \\
-                               & SCOTCH\_Num           & partnbr, \\
-                               & SCOTCH\_Num *         & parttab, \\
+                               & const SCOTCH\_Num     & partnbr, \\
+                               & const SCOTCH\_Num *   & parttab, \\
                                & FILE *                & stream
 \end{tabular}}
 
@@ -4099,7 +4099,7 @@ The \texttt{SCOTCH\_graphPartOvlView} routine writes to
 partition of the source graph \texttt{grafptr} into \texttt{partnbr}
 parts, as passed in \texttt{parttab}.
 See also \texttt{SCOTCH\_graphPartOvl},
-Section~\label{sec-lib-func-graphpartovl}.
+Section~\ref{sec-lib-func-graphpartovl}.
 
 Fortran users must use the \texttt{PXFFILENO} or \texttt{FNUM}
 functions to obtain the number of the Unix file descriptor
-- 
